 334: ## 6. Uniformity and bookkeeping (precisions supplied by this document)
 335: 
 336: - **U1 (small factors).** Trial division to B(N) is part of FACTOR. Every later estimate is applied to the
 337:   cofactor N′ with its own B(N′) ≤ B(N); N′ has no prime factor ≤ B(N) ≥ B(N′). If N′ < N₀ it is factored in
 338:   O(1) time. L_{N′} ≤ L_N.
 339: - **U2 (prime powers, perfect powers).** Removed before SPLIT; N′ = p^e is detected by integer roots plus AKS.
 340:   Non-squarefree N′ with ω ≥ 2 (e.g. p²q) needs no special treatment: DD uses |μ₂| = 2^ω, and FM/LD*/LV6
 341:   use only (N, t) = 1 and N | F(g₀, g₁).
 342: - **U3 (N₀).** Every "for N ≥ N₀" in the sources depends only on (d, k, μ, η₀, the σ-range). The effective
 343:   constants of Stark, Landau and Lagarias–Odlyzko make N₀ effective but huge ([lv6] §7).
 344: - **U4 (o(1) terms).** The L^{o(1)} factors are (log N)^{O(k)}, 2^{O(ω)}, γ^{−O(k)}, C(2k, k), and the Wiedemann
 345:   and Hensel polylogs. All are L^{o(1)} uniformly in N, because k is fixed and γ ≥ L^{−o(1)} (Step 5).
 346:   - With the computable S, γ is not ≥ 1/(log N)^{O(1)} ([label omitted]ed after codex thmA_1 §15).
 347:   - Pr(𝓡) = exp(−Ω(log N/log log N)) is still o(γ).
 348: - **U5 (S is computable).** Ψ is not computed by the algorithm. Any computable S with S = L^{θ/(4a)+o(1)} works:
 349:   FM gives E N = L^{o(1)} (possibly < 1, by an L^{o(1)} factor), LD*'s bound is uniform over S = L^{σ+o(1)},
 350:   and Prop PZ then gives γ ≥ L^{−o(1)} without E N ≥ 1. The cost T_SQ = S²L^{o(1)} is unchanged in exponent.
 351: - **U6 (sign of the split).** The Gauss-reduced (u₀, v₀) can have u₀v₀ < 0; sign(u₀v₀) belongs in q_i and is
 352:   killed by the sign column.
 353: - **U7 (expected time versus probability).** All loops are Las Vegas with verified outputs (kernel vectors,
 354:   η² = Γ, gcd), so only expected costs need bounding. LP's algorithm is used through its expected-time bound;
 355:   no cap is needed.
