 105: ## 3. The algorithm
 106: 
 107: All primality tests are AKS (deterministic polynomial time). "gcd check x" means: compute g = gcd(x, N); if
 108: 1 < g < N output g (a proper factor; recursion continues on g and N/g); if g = N reject the current object.
 109: 
 110: ```
 111: FACTOR(N):
 112:   if N = 1: return []
 113:   if N is prime (AKS): return [N]
 114:   if N = m^e for some e ≥ 2 (integer roots, e ≤ log2 N): return FACTOR(m) repeated e times
 115:   trial-divide N by all primes ≤ B(N); recurse on each prime found; let N' be the cofactor
 116:   if N' ∈ {1} or N' prime or N' a perfect power: handle as above
 117:   if N' < N₀(d,k,μ,η₀): factor N' by trial division (O(1) time)
 118:   g := SPLIT(N')           # 1 < g < N', g | N'
 119:   return FACTOR(g) ++ FACTOR(N'/g)
 120: 
 121: SPLIT(N):    # N > N₀, odd, every prime factor > B, not a prime power (so ω(N) ≥ 2)
 122:   # Phase F: field selection ([hypD] Corollary K, "retain the first field whose attempt succeeds")
 123:   loop:
 124:     A := SAMPLE_FIELD(N)                       # may exit with a proper factor
 125:     if A = REJECT: continue
 126:     row := DESCEND_ONCE(A, N)                  # may exit with a proper factor
 127:     if row ≠ FAIL: keep A; rows := [row]; break
 128:   # Phase R + L
 129:   loop:
 130:     while |rows| < M_rows: row := DESCEND_ONCE(A, N); if row ≠ FAIL: append row
 131:     (S, Y) := LV6(A, rows)                     # [lv6] Algorithm LV6 steps 1–6, Las Vegas
 132:     X := ∏_{i ∈ S} r_i mod N
 133:     g := gcd(X − Y, N); if 1 < g < N: return g
 134:     rows := []                                 # trivial gcd: fresh hidden roots, same field ([lv6] §3.7)
 135: 
 136: SAMPLE_FIELD(N):
 137:   draw (g0, g1) uniform in [M/2, M]^2 until gcd(g0, g1) = 1
 138:   draw w uniform among primes in (W, 2W] (uniform integers + AKS)
 139:   draw c uniform in [−H, H]^d
 140:   gcd checks: g1, w, then f_d = a_d + g1 c0 (0 < |f_d| < N)
 141:   f := F̂_{g,w}(x, 1) + (g1 x − g0) R_c(x, 1)        # Lemma GB on N·w
 142:   e := content(f);  e | N w;  if 1 < gcd(e, N) < N: output it;  if e = w: return REJECT   # e ∈ {1, w} otherwise
 143:   if no prime r ∈ (r0(d), ½ log H] gives an irreducible degree-d reduction f mod r: return REJECT   # Lemma IR
