 436: *Proof.*
 437: 0. Pairs with ℓ ∤ Δ contribute nothing. Since g is primitive, its reduction mod ℓ is nonzero, and two
 438:    vectors annihilated by the nonzero linear form x ↦ g₁x₁ − g₀x₂ mod ℓ have determinant ≡ 0 (mod ℓ).
 439: 1. g ↦ (G_g(P), G_g(P′)) is the integer matrix [[a, −b], [a′, −b′]] acting on (g₁, g₀). Its determinant
 440:    is −Δ ≠ 0, so the map is injective with image of index |Δ|.
 441: 2. L_ℓ(P) has index ℓ in Z². ℓ | Δ forces ℓ | G_g(P′) whenever ℓ | G_g(P), so L_ℓ(P) = L_ℓ(P′), and its
 442:    image lies in ℓZ² with index ℓ|Δ| in Z². Dividing by ℓ gives a lattice of index ℓ|Δ|/ℓ² = q.
 443: 3. b·G_g(P′) − b′·G_g(P) = g₁(ba′ − b′a) = −g₁Δ, so bn′ − b′n = ∓g₁q ≡ 0 (mod q). The image therefore
 444:    lies in Γ_q, which also has index q, so the two are equal. ∎
