 401:     E_{ℓ,w}Σ_{P≠P′, ℓ|Δ}|𝒢|^{−1}Σ_g Y_PY_{P′}(S²/q)κ_alg ≤ (log N)^{O(1)}S⁴ρ_r².
 402:   This uses (S²/q)κ_alg ≍ Z/(4d²H²V^{2d−4}ϱ(T|G|)ϱ(T|G′|)) and ϱ(T|G|) ≥ ρ_F/(log N)^{O(1)} under the filter.
 403: - With FM: PC ≤ (log N)^{O(1)}, so D_k(γ) holds with γ ≥ L^{−o(1)} (Prop PZ).
 404: 
 405: *Proof.* Put T := dHV^{d−1}, t := |G_g(P)|, t′ := |G_g(P′)| and q := |Δ|/ℓ ∈ [1, 2S²]. Pair sums run over ordered
 406: pairs P ≠ P′ in 𝒫_ℓ ∩ Λ_ℓ(g), with ℓ | Δ and both filtered.
 407: - **Step 0 (law).** For ℓ | N, N_ℓ := 0. For ℓ ∤ N, under 𝒜‴,
 408:     E[N(N−1)] = E_{ℓ,g,w} Σ_{P≠P′} Y_PY_{P′}·Pr_c[F_A(P), F_A(P′) ∈ 𝒮_B].
 409:   - Pairs with ℓ ∤ Δ contribute nothing (pcest Lemma Q, step 0).
 410:   - Only F̂_{g,w} depends on w.
 411: - **Step 1 (kernel).**
 412:   - Lemma Kern(iii), with ‖v ∧ v′‖ ≥ |Δ|(bb′)^{d−2} ≥ |Δ|(V/2)^{2d−4}, gives Pr_c[Φ(c) = z] ≤ C_d/(H²V^{2d−4}).
 413:   - Φ(C_H) ⊂ [−T, T]², and Γ = {z₂ ≡ κ^{d−1}z₁ (mod Δ)} (Kern(i)), where P′ ≡ κP (mod Δ). Hence
 414:       Pr_c[both smooth] ≤ (C_d/(H²V^{2d−4}))·Z,  Z := Σ_{j mod |Δ|} A_j(P)A_{κ^{d−1}j}(P′),
 415:     with A_j(P) := #{|z| ≤ T : z ≡ j (mod |Δ|), F̂(P) + G(P)z ∈ 𝒮_B}.
 416: - **Step 2 (AM–GM).**
 417:   - κ is a unit mod Δ, since P′ is primitive.
 418:   - So Z ≤ ½(Q(P) + Q(P′)), with Q(P) := Σ_j A_j(P)², which depends on (P, g, w, |Δ|) only.
 419:   - The inequality is pointwise but one-sided (Z may vanish while Q > 0). Both sides have the same
 420:     main-term scale.
 421: - **Step 3 (enlargement).**
 422:   - z ↦ F = F̂(P) + G(P)z is injective, with F ≡ r₀ (mod t). Also z ≡ z′ (mod |Δ|) ⟺ F ≡ F′ (mod t|Δ|), for
 423:     either sign of G. All such F lie in [−X*, X*] (§1). Hence
 424:       Q(P) ≤ 𝔔₀(t, |Δ|; r₀) := #{(F, F′) ∈ 𝒮*² : F ≡ F′ ≡ r₀ (mod t), F ≡ F′ (mod t|Δ|)}.
 425:   - 𝔔₀ is a fixed function of r₀ that does not depend on w.
 426:   - Under the filter, tT ≍_d X*, so the enlargement has bounded scale.
 427: - **Step 4 (average over w).**
 428:   - Both candidates have Y = 1, so (1.1) and Corollary W apply. The classes c partition the counted
 429:     pairs, so
 430:       E_w 𝔔₀(t, |Δ|; r₀) ≤ (C_W/φ(t)) Σ_{c∈(Z/t)^×} 𝔔₀(t, |Δ|; c) ≤ (C_W/φ(t))·𝔔(t|Δ|).
 431:   - The same holds for P′.
