 436:   - Fix ℓ, P = (a, b) and P′ with |Δ| = ℓq. The algebraic factor 𝔔(tℓq)/φ(t) depends on g only through
 437:     n := G_g(P)/ℓ, and Y_P = 1 ⟺ n ∈ 𝒩_ℓ.
 438:   - For fixed n, the g with G_g(P) = ℓn are g = g* + j(a, b) in (g₀, g₁)-coordinates. The direction is
 439:     primitive with |(a, b)| > V/2, so there are ≤ √2M/V + 1 values of j.
