  70: 
  71: Notation.
  72: - P⁺(n) and P⁻(n) are the largest and smallest prime factors of n, with P⁺(1) = 1 and P⁻(1) = +∞.
  73: - S(z, y) is the set of y-smooth n ≤ z, Ψ(z, y) = #S(z, y), and ϱ(z, y) := Ψ(z, y)/z.
  74: - For a Dirichlet character χ of any modulus, Ψ(z, y; χ) := Σ_{n∈S(z,y)} χ(n). Here χ(n) = 0 when
  75:   (n, mod χ) > 1.
  76: - For (a, q) = 1: Ψ(z, y; q, a) := #{n ∈ S(z, y) : n ≡ a (mod q)}, Ψ_q(z, y) := #{n ∈ S(z, y) :
  77:   (n, q) = 1}, and E(z, y; q, a) := Ψ(z, y; q, a) − Ψ_q(z, y)/φ(q).
  78: - u := log x/log y, and H(u) := exp(u/log²(u + 1)) (Drappeau's normalisation).
  79: - α(z, y) is the Hildebrand–Tenenbaum saddle point: the solution of Σ_{p≤y} log p/(p^α − 1) = log z.
  80: - L = L_N[1/2, 1] = exp((log N log log N)^{1/2}).
